<InstitutionalPage
  title="Editorial Standards"
  eyebrow="Standards"
  description="Nuvellum separates reporting, analysis, opinion, reviews and sponsored work, with stronger verification for sensitive claims."
  intro="The format, source discipline and level of verification should be visible in the published work—not hidden behind the interface."
  note="These standards apply across Nuvellum’s newsroom and to every published format."
>
  <h2>Labels are part of the reporting</h2>
  <p>News, analysis, opinion, reviews and sponsored work are labeled separately. Reporting should not quietly inherit the voice or certainty of commentary, and sponsored material should not resemble independent editorial judgment.</p>
  <h2>Sources and attribution</h2>
  <p>Reporting should retain sufficient source records for the underlying material to be traced. Contested claims, allegations and interpretations should be attributed rather than adopted as Nuvellum’s own voice.</p>
  <h2>Sensitive stories</h2>
  <p>Political, legal, conflict, serious-harm and other high-risk stories require an independent verification result before publication. A story that does not clear that step is held rather than softened into publication.</p>
  <h2>Editorial responsibility</h2>
  <p>Publication decisions remain subject to the same standards of sourcing, attribution, verification and correction regardless of format or desk.</p>
</InstitutionalPage>
